<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		Open devtools to observe the class names of "Partly selected".
		1. Click "Partly selected": it becomes checked.
		- Expected: it carries z-checkbox-on, no longer z-checkbox-indeterminate.
		- Bug: z-checkbox-indeterminate stays, so a theme drawing the state by class keeps the minus sign.
		2. Untick it, then tick "Make the first one indeterminate" (the server calls setIndeterminate(true)).
		- Expected: "Partly selected" carries z-checkbox-indeterminate again.
		- Bug: no z-checkbox-indeterminate class is added in the default mold.
		3. Click "Tristate" three times: its class must follow indeterminate, on, off as before;
			"Tristate, partly" starts indeterminate.
		4. Reload, then run zk.Widget.$('$cb').setChecked(true) in the console:
			"Partly selected" must carry z-checkbox-on, without z-checkbox-indeterminate.
		With the WCAG module:
		5. Click "clear indeterminate" (the server calls setIndeterminate(false)), before or after step 2:
			"Partly selected" must carry aria-checked="false", not "mixed".
		6. Toggle "Switch": aria-checked of its mold (role="switch") must follow.
	</label>
	<vlayout>
		<checkbox id="cb" label="Partly selected" indeterminate="true"/>
		<checkbox id="other" label="Make the first one indeterminate"
			onCheck='cb.setChecked(false); cb.setIndeterminate(true)'/>
		<checkbox id="tri" mold="tristate" label="Tristate"/>
		<checkbox id="triMixed" mold="tristate" indeterminate="true" label="Tristate, partly"/>
		<button id="log" label="log server state" onClick='Clients.log("" + cb.getState() + "," + tri.getState())'/>
		<button id="clear" label="clear indeterminate" onClick="cb.setIndeterminate(false)"/>
		<checkbox id="sw" mold="switch" label="Switch"/>
	</vlayout>
</zk>
